 myth came first, and the bones merely seemed to confirm it.", "orig": "The idea found a champion in Adrienne Mayor, a Stanford folklorist and historian of science. In The First Fossil Hunters, she argues that Greeks and Romans noticed big fossil bones, collected them, measured them, and tried to explain them. Giants, and one-eyed monsters, may owe something to those finds. On the Cyclops, though, Mayor herself is careful. She does not like to say the fossils were the source of the story, 'because we just can't prove that.' We do not know, she says, which came first. Perhaps the myth came first, and the bones merely seemed to confirm it."}